.\"  -*- nroff -*-
.Dd October 16, 2026
.Dt MCD 8 SMM
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mcd
.Nd IGMP and MLD querier for the Linux bridge
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl hnstv
.Op Fl f Ar FILE
.Op Fl i Ar NAME
.Op Fl l Ar LEVEL
.Op Fl p Ar FILE
.Op Fl u Ar FILE
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a multicast querier for the Linux bridge.  It runs one IGMP and one
MLD querier on every interface enabled in
.Xr mcd.conf 5 ,
either the bridge itself or a VLAN interface on top of it.
.Pp
Snooping in the bridge only works while there is a querier on the LAN.
Without one, the bridge floods all multicast to every port.  The bridge
has a querier of its own, but it runs one fixed protocol version, sends
IGMP queries from 0.0.0.0 unless set to use its own address, and then
uses one address for all VLANs.  Some end devices ignore queries from
0.0.0.0.  When they do, their memberships expire and they lose their
stream.
.Nm
fills that gap:
.Bl -bullet -offset indent
.It
IGMP queries are sent from the interface address, MLD queries from
its link-local address, as RFC 2710 and RFC 3810 require.
.It
Querier election per RFC 2236, 3376, 2710 and 3810, the lowest address
wins.  When another querier wins,
.Nm
backs off and takes over again if it goes silent for the
.Cm router-timeout .
.It
On assuming the querier role,
.Nm
sends a startup burst of
.Cm robustness
queries,
.Cm query-interval
/ 4 apart, RFC 3376 \(sc8.6 and \(sc8.7.
.It
Starts at IGMPv3 and MLDv2 and falls back to IGMPv2, IGMPv1 or MLDv1
for as long as older hosts are heard.
.It
Proxy mode, a backup querier that always loses the election.  An
interface without an address is always in proxy mode.
.It
Raw VLAN mode, a querier on one VLAN of a VLAN filtering bridge with no
VLAN interface on top.
.It
Static groups, joined in the kernel so the bridge always forwards them
to itself.
.El
.Pp
Interfaces, links and addresses are followed with netlink, so an
interface that appears late or gets its address from DHCP needs no
restart.
.Pp
Use
.Xr mctl 8
to inspect a running
.Nm .
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl f , -config Ns = Ns Ar FILE
Configuration file, default derived from the identity, see
.Fl i
and
.Sx FILES .
.It Fl h , -help
Show usage, including the default paths, and exit.
.It Fl i , -ident Ns = Ns Ar NAME
Identity, default
.Nm .
Sets the syslog tag and the default names of the configuration, PID and
IPC socket files.  Use one identity per instance to run several, and
the same with
.Xr mctl 8 .
.It Fl l , -loglevel Ns = Ns Ar LEVEL
Log level, one of
.Cm none , err , notice , info
or
.Cm debug .
Default
.Cm notice .
.It Fl n , -foreground
Run in the foreground, log to stderr.
.It Fl p , -pidfile Ns = Ns Ar FILE
PID file, default derived from the identity.  The file is touched when
a reload completes.
.It Fl s , -syslog
Log to syslog, the default unless
.Fl n
is given.
.It Fl t , -check-config
Check the configuration file and exit without starting the daemon.
Errors are reported as
.Ar FILE:LINE: message
with a non-zero exit status.  Runs as a normal user.
.It Fl u , -ipc Ns = Ns Ar FILE
IPC socket used by
.Xr mctl 8 ,
default derived from the identity.
.It Fl v , -version
Show version and exit.
.El
.Sh SIGNALS
.Bl -tag -width TERM
.It HUP
Reload the configuration file and probe all interfaces again.  Static
group memberships and packet sockets that are still configured are
kept, so a reload causes no traffic on the wire.  The PID file is
touched when done.
.It INT , TERM
Exit.  Static group memberships are dropped, the kernel sends the
leaves.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width MCD_SOCK
.It Ev MCD_SOCK
IPC socket path, overridden by
.Fl u .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /run/mcd.sock -compact
.It Pa /etc/mcd.conf
Configuration file, see
.Xr mcd.conf 5 .
.It Pa /run/mcd.pid
PID file.
.It Pa /run/mcd.sock
IPC socket.
.El
.Pp
The names follow the identity, so
.Fl i Ar foo
uses
.Pa /etc/foo.conf
and so on.  The directories are set at build time.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mcd.conf 5 ,
.Xr bridge 8 ,
.Xr mctl 8
.Sh STANDARDS
.Rs
.%R RFC 2236
.%T Internet Group Management Protocol, Version 2
.Re
.Rs
.%R RFC 3376
.%T Internet Group Management Protocol, Version 3
.Re
.Rs
.%R RFC 2710
.%T Multicast Listener Discovery (MLD) for IPv6
.Re
.Rs
.%R RFC 3810
.%T Multicast Listener Discovery Version 2 (MLDv2) for IPv6
.Re
.Rs
.%R RFC 5790
.%T Lightweight IGMPv3 and MLDv2 Protocols
.Re
.Sh HISTORY
.Nm
began in 2021 as querierd, written by
.An Joachim Wiberg
at Westermo with DNA strands from mrouted.  It gave the Linux bridge in
WeOS 5 a querier that industrial end devices would actually answer.
Westermo's last release of querierd was v0.10, in May 2023.
.Pp
In 2024 its original author adopted it as
.Nm .
Version 2.0 replaced the last of the mrouted code, and version 3.0 added
the MLD querier.  Today
.Nm
is the multicast querier in Infix OS.
